# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What must never be published.
#
# This working tree is ~56 GB and contains a live product's operational data.
# Everything excluded here is either enormous, regenerable, third-party, or
# private. Read the reasons before removing a line.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PRIVATE — learner data. Offsite DB exports: real people's email addresses and
# every word of coursework they submitted. Never publish.
backups/

# Third-party. MoneyPrinterTurbo is a separate MIT-licensed project kept as a
# clean clone for `git pull` (45 GB with its venv). It is a dependency, not our
# source — see README for how to obtain it.
MoneyPrinterTurbo/

# Rendered course videos: 10.6 GB, regenerable from the factory.
studio/output/

# Generated pipeline artifacts.
studio/queue/pending/
studio/queue/done/
graphify-out/

# Raw source material and personal working files that are not build inputs.
# (The research the factory actually reads lives in studio/research/.)
liv-docs/
researches/
*.docx
resumen_carrera_influencer_marketing.pdf

# CVs. Real ones, belonging to real people, used to calibrate the CV matcher
# (docs/10) the way docs/07 demands — against real documents, never ones we
# wrote ourselves. This repo is PUBLIC, so they must never be committed: they
# carry names, phone numbers and employment history that are not ours to
# publish. Keep them local; the fixture set that IS committed lives in
# studio/fixtures/cvs/ and is redacted.
*.pdf
!brag-output/**/*.pdf
cvs/

# Video composition working files. The finished cut is committed; the 114 MB
# Chrome cache and node_modules behind it are not.
brag-output/composition/node_modules/
brag-output/composition/renders/
brag-output/*.jpg
!brag-output/brag.jpg

# Secrets. This project reads every credential from Railway at runtime and has
# no secrets in source — this is a tripwire, not a cleanup.
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem
config.toml

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Third-party audio. The music bed and SFX ship with the /brag plugin, whose own
# README says redistribution terms must be verified first — they have not been.
# The rendered video embeds them (ordinary use of a bundled asset); the raw
# tracks are not ours to republish. See brag-output/README.md to restore them.
brag-output/composition/assets/audio/

# The frontend workspace (studio/web): the test suite now, the Astro app next.
# The lockfile IS tracked — the Docker build stage must be reproducible.
studio/web/node_modules/
studio/web/dist/
studio/web/.astro/

# Frontend build output copied into the image by Docker stage 1.
studio/dashboard/static/web/
